msgid "[qiskit/granite-3.3-8b-qiskit-GGUF](https://huggingface.co/Qiskit/granite-3.3-8b-qiskit-GGUF) – Released **June 2025**  \n"
msgstr "[qiskit/granite-3.3-8b-qiskit-GGUF](https://huggingface.co/Qiskit/granite-3.3-8b-qiskit-GGUF) – Wydany **w czerwcu 2025**  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[qiskit/granite-3.2-8b-qiskit-GGUF](https://huggingface.co/Qiskit/granite-3.2-8b-qiskit-GGUF) – Released **June 2025**  \n"
msgstr "[qiskit/granite-3.2-8b-qiskit-GGUF](https://huggingface.co/Qiskit/granite-3.2-8b-qiskit-GGUF) – Wydany **w czerwcu 2025**  \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Open Source Qiskit Code Assistant models are available in <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Safetensors is a file format designed specifically for storing machine learning model weights and tensors in a secure and efficient manner.\">safetensors</DefinitionTooltip> or <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"GGUF is a binary format that is designed for quickly loading and saving models, and for readability.\">GGUF file format</DefinitionTooltip> and can be downloaded from the Hugging Face as explained below.\n"
msgstr "Modele Qiskit Code Assistant o otwartym kodzie źródłowym są dostępne w formacie <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Safetensors is a file format designed specifically for storing machine learning model weights and tensors in a secure and efficient manner.\">safetensors</DefinitionTooltip> lub <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"GGUF is a binary format that is designed for quickly loading and saving models, and for readability.\">GGUF</DefinitionTooltip> i można je pobrać z Hugging Face, jak wyjaśniono poniżej.\n"

